"content":[{"text":"He sold out two consecutive nights at Yankee Stadium in July 2014, the first Latin solo artist to headline it, and on 21 September 2019 filled MetLife Stadium with some sixty thousand people, again the first, releasing the night as «Utopía Live from MetLife Stadium». «Fórmula, Vol. 3: La Gira» ran eighty-eight shows through 2023.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"3a7c19e8-5d24-4f06-b8e1-9c4a70f2d5b3","displayText":"Aventura","occurrenceId":"37e0d22e-5fb2-4d72-b8b2-f448e30b1a21"}},{"text":" reunited for a farewell tour, «Cerrando Ciclos», which closed on 5 January 2025 at the Estadio Olímpico Félix Sánchez in Santo Domingo before more than fifty thousand people, the last of four sold-out nights in the country. In November 2025 Santos released «Better Late Than Never», a surprise joint album with ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"9c02d1a1-952e-4855-9b60-c0266236378d","displayText":"Prince Royce","occurrenceId":"1611aefd-b2a1-48ea-aef8-12c4c1e6017a"}},{"text":", and the two opened the «Mejor Tarde Que Nunca» tour in April 2026.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"The songwriter","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Santos wrote almost the whole ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"3a7c19e8-5d24-4f06-b8e1-9c4a70f2d5b3","displayText":"Aventura","occurrenceId":"fd92795e-3cf1-4641-b3b1-34ac29677142"}},{"text":" catalogue — the group recorded one cover in its career — and has written for others throughout. «No, No, No», written and sung with Thalía, won pop song of the year at «Premios Lo Nuestro» in 2007. For ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"dee014d6-cb3c-4abb-9262-165538277a0d","displayText":"Héctor Acosta “El Torito”","occurrenceId":"fa6d71f9-c9f2-4ef8-86c4-0d82d9c6fafa"}},{"text":" he wrote «Me voy», a bachata rewrite of an ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"3a7c19e8-5d24-4f06-b8e1-9c4a70f2d5b3","displayText":"Aventura","occurrenceId":"61c5354f-c807-4a69-8e9a-09e301d8d545"}},{"text":" merengue, and «Amorcito enfermito», a number one on the Tropical Airplay chart in 2016; in 2020 he cut a duet version of «Nuestro Amor» with ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"6c3e0d74-23b7-4d80-969f-9d5319ee5127","displayText":"Alex Bueno","occurrenceId":"432ebd06-d3bd-4d68-8ba7-cbeb8b75712d"}},{"text":". He was named songwriter of the year at the «Billboard» Latin Music Awards in 2007 and from 2014 to 2016, and producer of the year in 2014 and 2015.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Legacy","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"3a7c19e8-5d24-4f06-b8e1-9c4a70f2d5b3","displayText":"Aventura","occurrenceId":"1aaff5fa-138a-48f4-95d6-7e5d0ae2c5b5"}},{"text":" is the point at which bachata stopped being a Dominican genre exported abroad and became one written abroad and sold back home. Santos holds a Latin Grammy, three «Billboard» Music Awards and nineteen «Premios Lo Nuestro», which gave him its excellence award in 2017, and ACROARTE named him El Gran Soberano in 2021 — its highest distinction, for a Dominican career, given to a man born in New York.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"«Utopía» is the clearest statement of what he does with that position: having become the most commercially successful bachatero in the genre''s history, he spent an album handing the microphone back to ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"0760875d-6b6f-4a48-8aed-6e57934d1baa","displayText":"Luis Vargas","occurrenceId":"44336eec-06b4-409f-aea3-dbb6cd26bc94"}},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"28a3745e-90d6-45cd-b8bd-798028f8deb8","displayText":"Antony Santos","occurrenceId":"5ff0e13e-a7aa