"text":":","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"text":" Wrote and arranged several tracks, including «El viejo» and «El grillo».","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Commercial Success and \"La Voz de Mantequilla\"","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"In the late 1990s, almost by accident, Freddy Gerardo launched his own musical project as a frontman and lead singer. While recording guide vocals for his demo tapes, he jokingly referred to himself as \"La Voz de Mantequilla\" (\"The Butter Voice\").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Signed under the label ","type":"text"},{"text":"Allegro Productions","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":" (led by Johnny Montaño, Manolo Ascona, and Papo Daniel Hernández), he introduced a festive and humorous style that revolutionized the merengue scene of the era:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"«Dame del Pollito» (El Pollito):","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"text":" Inspired by the rhythms of the baton twirling groups (","type":"text"},{"text":"batón ballet","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":") from his hometown, this track became a massive global radio and commercial hit. The song''s impact was so significant that the British network BBC traveled to the Dominican Republic to film a report on him.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Other Hits:","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"text":" Popularized several catchphrases and comedic tracks such as «El Maco», «El Perro Chihuahua», «El Chivo», «La Pelota», and «La Chuleta».","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}'::jsonb, revision = revision + 1, updated_at = now() WHERE id = (SELECT d.id FROM editorial_documents d JOIN artists a ON a.id = d.owner_artist_id WHERE a.slug = 'freddy-gerardo' AND d.locale = 'en' AND